Here is the full solution.

function largestNumber(numbers) {
  if (numbers.length === 0) {
    return null;
  }
  let largest = numbers[0];
  for (const n of numbers) {
    if (n > largest) {
      largest = n;
    }
  }
  return largest;
}

Starting from the first item (not 0) keeps negative arrays correct, and the early return handles the empty array.
